From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:25:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: don't schedule the main phy twice per tx worker
 run

Since "add multi-radio support to tx scheduling", mt76_tx_worker_run()
schedules dev->phy explicitly before walking dev->phys[]. On drivers
without separate radio phys, dev->phys[MT_BAND0] is dev->phy itself, so
band 0 got a second, mostly empty scheduling pass over all ACs on every
run, and other bands waited behind it.

Skip dev->phy in the loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tx.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index dc6a65d3..0060cfa8 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -785,7 +785,8 @@ void mt76_tx_worker_run(struct mt76_dev *dev)
 	mt76_txq_schedule_all(&dev->phy);
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->phys); i++) {
 		phy = dev->phys[i];
-		if (!phy)
+		/* unless replaced by a radio phy, phys[0] is dev->phy */
+		if (!phy || phy == &dev->phy)
 			continue;
 
 		mt76_txq_schedule_all(phy);
